<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:local="using:PhotoBook.Shell.Views"
             xmlns:controls="using:PhotoBook.Shell.Controls"
             x:Class="PhotoBook.Shell.Views.ProjectListView"
             FontFamily="Inter">

    <!--
        Transcribed from doc\DESIGN_SPEC.md section 3, number by number, the same way the
        header was. Nothing here is a value looked at by eye:

            header card  padding 24, radius 16, white, slate-200/80 border, shadow-subtle
            title        20 bold            subtitle 12, slate-500, 2 above
            create       16/10, radius 12, brand-600, 12 semibold
            grid         at most 3 columns, gap 24
            card         padding 20, radius 16, same border and shadow
            status pill  padding 11/5, radius 10, border 1, 12 semibold, dot 6
            time         11, slate-400
            name         16 bold
            mode chip    8 left, radius 8, padding 9/4, border 1
            stats        16 above / 12 below a slate-100 rule, two columns 8 apart
            footer       20 above / 12 below a slate-100 rule, 8 apart
            open         8/12, radius 12, slate-100, 12 semibold
            delete       8, radius 12, glyph 14, slate-400 turning red-500 on red-50

        The pill radius is 10 rather than the 6 the mockup asked for: at 22 pixels tall a
        radius of 6 still reads as a rectangle patch, and more rounding was asked for. One
        number if that changes.

        Every command on a card is bound to the screen's data context rather than to the item,
        with the item as the parameter. Binding a command that lives on the item would mean
        every card was its own little view model, and the list is one.
    -->
    <Grid MaxWidth="1600" Margin="32,24" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">

        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!--
            ============================ control panel ==========================

            One row, three things: what this screen is, what you want to see, and the one
            action you can take.

            The filters were a separate bar and the panel looked empty without them, which
            is the wrong way round: the filters are how you choose what to see ON this
            screen, so they belong to this screen's panel, and a panel that only carries a
            heading is a heading pretending to be a panel.

            It is a single row on purpose. Nothing in it is taller than the heading was, so
            the panel gives back no vertical space - which matters more than usual here,
            because the thing below it is a grid of cards and every pixel of height is a
            row of photographs the photographer can see.
        -->
        <Border Grid.Row="0" Classes="card" Padding="20"
                IsVisible="{Binding ProjectsCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}">
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto" MinHeight="52">

                <!-- The heading. -->
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,20,0">
                    <TextBlock Text="Проекты фотокниг" Classes="t20Bold" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="t12" Margin="0,2,0,0"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                               Text="Управляйте подготовленными макетами и запускайте их в автоматический экспорт" />
                </StackPanel>

                <!--
                    The two questions: which editor, and how far along. Two, because those
                    are the two anybody asks with twenty projects in the folder. The words
                    are the card badges' own words - see ProjectStatusText - so a card can
                    never come back saying something different from the filter that chose it.

                    These are borderless on purpose. Inside a white panel a boxed control
                    reads as a foreign object dropped in; borderless reads as belonging, and
                    it takes its shape from the pointer on hover instead of from a frame.
                -->
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">

                    <controls:FilterDropDown AutomationName="Фильтр по режиму"
                                              ToolTip.Tip="Каким редактором собран проект"
                                              Items="{Binding ModeChoices}"
                                              SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedMode, Mode=TwoWay}" />

                    <controls:FilterDropDown AutomationName="Фильтр по статусу"
                                              ToolTip.Tip="Как готово собрание"
                                              Items="{Binding StatusChoices}"
                                              SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedStatus, Mode=TwoWay}" />

                    <!-- Appears only when something is being filtered out, so it is never a
                         control that is there and does nothing. -->
                    <Button Classes="ghostClear" IsVisible="{Binding IsNarrowed}"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Сбросить фильтры"
                            ToolTip.Tip="Показать все проекты"
                            Command="{Binding ClearFiltersCommand}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Сбросить" />
                    </Button>

                    <!-- The count, in words. A bare number next to two filters reads as "the
                         filter returned 39", which is a different and wrong thing to
                         believe; while narrowing it reads "7 из 39", which is honest about
                         both numbers. -->
                    <!--
                         A fixed width, so the filters beside it do not move.

                         The count grows and shrinks with the answer it gives -
                         "Всего: 39", "8 из 39", "39 из 39" - and because the group is
                         pushed to the right of the panel, every one of those widths
                         shoved the two filters left and right by a few pixels. The
                         filters were fixed first and the count was then the last thing
                         still moving them, which is the same fault one element over.

                         Seventy pixels is the width of the longest of the three, so
                         every answer sits in the same box and the filters stand still.
                         The words are right-aligned inside it, so the figures line up
                         with each other rather than hanging off its left edge.
                     -->
                    <TextBlock Text="{Binding FilterSummary}" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               Margin="12,0,0,0" Classes="t12" MinWidth="70"
                               TextAlignment="Right"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                </StackPanel>

                <!--
                    The one action on the screen.

                    It is deliberately the same weight as the export button on the other
                    screens rather than the loudest thing in the window: the photographer is
                    mostly looking, and the loudest control on a screen is the one they get
                    invited to press. Thirty-eight pixels, a hair of breathing room either
                    side of the mark, and states for the pointer - a filled button that gives
                    nothing back when pressed does not feel pressed, which is most of why it
                    used to look unfinished.
                -->
                <Button Grid.Column="2" Classes="createProject" Margin="20,0,0,0"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Создать проект"
                        Command="{Binding CreateProjectCommand}">
                    <!--
                        Text, and only text.

                        The mark beside it was a thin plus in a dark shade on a dark fill -
                        it was barely there, and what it added was a second thing to look at
                        in the one control a person should not have to look at twice. The
                        word alone is unambiguous in any language this program is used in,
                        and it sits centred because there is nothing else in the control to
                        align it with.
                    -->
                    <TextBlock Text="Создать проект" Foreground="White"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Button>
            </Grid>
        </Border>

        <!-- The empty screen gets the panel's heading on its own; there is nothing to filter.

             Same 52 pixels of content as the panel above it, and that is the whole point.
             Without it this panel was five pixels shorter, and the two are swapped for one
             another every time the list is opened: ProjectsCount is briefly nothing while
             the projects are read, so the short one appeared for a moment and the panel
             visibly shrank and then grew back. A panel that changes height when you come
             back to it looks like the program is still loading; it was, but it should not
             be something you can watch. -->
        <Border Grid.Row="0" Classes="card" Padding="20"
                IsVisible="{Binding ProjectsCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}, ConverterParameter=empty}">
            <StackPanel MinHeight="52">
                <TextBlock Text="Проекты фотокниг" Classes="t20Bold" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                <TextBlock Classes="t12" Margin="0,2,0,0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                           Text="Управляйте подготовленными макетами и запускайте их в автоматический экспорт" />
            </StackPanel>
        </Border>

        <!-- ================================ body ============================== -->
        <Panel Grid.Row="2" Margin="0,24,0,0">

            <!-- No loading plate, and there is nothing to load.
                 The list used to open and parse every project file to draw the cards, so a
                 plate over the grid was honest about what was happening - except that it was
                 painted UNDER the cards, so it never covered anything and only showed
                 through the gaps as a tint that vanished when loading ended. The cost it was
                 warning about is gone: the list reads the index, and a plate that flashes
                 for three milliseconds is worse than no plate at all. -->

            <!-- error banner -->
            <Border IsVisible="{Binding ErrorMessage, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}"
                    Background="#FEF2F2" BorderBrush="#FECACA" BorderThickness="1"
                    CornerRadius="12" Padding="16,12" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ErrorMessage}" Classes="t12"
                           Foreground="#DC2626" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            </Border>

            <!-- empty state: gone the moment there is one project -->

            <!--
                A filter that matched nothing, which is a different thing from having no
                projects at all. The empty state below says "create your first project",
                which is nonsense to somebody with thirty of them - so the two are kept
                apart, and this one offers the way back instead.
            -->
            <Border IsVisible="{Binding HasNoMatches}" MaxWidth="520"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    Classes="card" Padding="24">
                <StackPanel Spacing="14" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock Text="Ничего не найдено" Classes="t16Bold" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="t12" TextAlignment="Center"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                               Text="Ни один проект не подходит под выбранные условия" />
                    <Button Classes="createProject" AutomationProperties.Name="Сбросить фильтры пусто"
                            Command="{Binding ClearFiltersCommand}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Сбросить фильтры" Foreground="White" />
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
            <Border Classes="card" Padding="24" MaxWidth="520"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    IsVisible="{Binding ProjectsCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}, ConverterParameter=empty}">
                <StackPanel Spacing="16" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                    <Border Width="56" Height="56" CornerRadius="16"
                            Background="{DynamicResource Brand50}"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE8C0;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="24"
                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Brand600}"
                                   HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </Border>
                    <TextBlock Text="Проектов пока нет" Classes="t18Bold"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="t12" TextWrapping="Wrap" TextAlignment="Center"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                               Text="Создайте первый проект, выберите режим вёрстки и загрузите фотографии." />
                    <Button Classes="primary" Padding="16,10"
                            HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                            AutomationProperties.Name="Создать первый проект"
                            Command="{Binding CreateProjectCommand}">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                            <TextBlock Text="&#xE710;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="12"
                                       Foreground="White" />
                            <TextBlock Text="Создать проект" Foreground="White" />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>

            <!-- the cards -->
            <!--
                 A scroll viewer, not a decoration. With twenty projects the grid is taller
                 than the window, and a screen that silently cuts its own list is a screen
                 that looks like it has six projects.
            -->
            <!--
                 The negative right margin is the scrollbar's place. It used to
                 take ten pixels out of the list, which is why the block of cards
                 stopped short of the control panel above it even though both measured
                 the same. Pushed out past the edge, it sits in the margin the window
                 already has, and the cards line up with the panel.
             -->
            <!--
                 The scrollbar's place.

                 It used to take ten pixels out of the list, which is why the block of
                 cards stopped short of the control panel above it even though both
                 measured the same. It is pushed out past the edge and given room of
                 its own: the margin is the scrollbar's width plus a gap, and the
                 padding hands the gap back, so the cards finish exactly at the
                 panel's edge and the scrollbar hangs in the window's own margin
                 instead of pressed against the last card.
             -->
            <ScrollViewer Classes="projectsScroll"
                          VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                          HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                          Margin="0,0,-20,0">
                <Border Padding="0,0,20,0">
                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding FilteredProjects}">
                <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                    <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                    <!-- Three columns, every card in a row as tall as the tallest card beside it.
                     The platform's uniform grid makes every cell in the list one height and
                     clips the long ones; a wrapping panel makes each card its own height and
                     an empty project comes out visibly shorter than its neighbours. Neither
                     is what the other shell does - it puts three columns in a grid and lets
                     each row be as tall as that row needs. That is the whole of what this
                     panel is. -->
                        <local:ThreeColumnPanel />
                    </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                        <Border Classes="card" Padding="20" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                            <!--
                                The content sits at the top and the button comes straight after
                                it. Pinning the button to the bottom of the card was tried and
                                undone against the released program: a card with no photographs in
                                it has its button high up there, and that is what people know.
                                Every card in a row is as tall as the row needs, so the slack is
                                at the bottom of the card - and it is the card's own slack, not a
                                hole left to be filled.
                            -->
                            <StackPanel>

                                <!-- status pill + when it changed -->
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*">
                                    <Border Grid.Column="0" CornerRadius="10" Padding="11,5"
                                            BorderThickness="1"
                                            Background="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToBrush}, ConverterParameter=bg}"
                                            BorderBrush="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToBrush}, ConverterParameter=border}">
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                                            <Ellipse Width="6" Height="6" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                     Fill="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToLabel}, ConverterParameter=dot}" />
                                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Semi" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       Foreground="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToBrush}, ConverterParameter=text}"
                                                       Text="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToLabel}}" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Border>

                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Classes="t11"
                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}"
                                               HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                               Text="{Binding LastModified, Converter={StaticResource LastModifiedText}, ConverterParameter=prefix}" />
                                </Grid>

                                <!-- name + which mode it belongs to -->
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="t16Bold"
                                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               Text="{Binding Name}" />

                                    <Border Grid.Column="1" Margin="8,0,0,0" CornerRadius="8"
                                            Padding="9,4" BorderThickness="1"
                                            VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                            IsVisible="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=visibility}"
                                            Background="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tintbg}"
                                            BorderBrush="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tintborder}">
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5">
                                            <TextBlock FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="11"
                                                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       Foreground="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tinticon}"
                                                       Text="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=icon}" />
                                            <TextBlock Classes="t11Semi" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       Foreground="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tinttext}"
                                                       Text="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}}" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Border>
                                </Grid>
                                  <!--
                                      Three 48px previews and the remainder.

                                      This row is a FIXED height and is always there.
                                      That is the whole of the fix for cards changing
                                      size: before, the row disappeared with the
                                      photographs, so a card with none in it was shorter -
                                      and since every card in a row is arranged to the
                                      height of the tallest among them, the same card was
                                      one size on its own and another size beside one
                                      that had photographs. The grid changed shape
                                      depending on what happened to be in the projects.

                                      The space is reserved, and an empty project shows
                                      that space and nothing else - no frames, no
                                      placeholders. A photograph that has not been put
                                      in yet is not a thing to draw a box around.
                                  -->
                                  <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,16,0,0"
                                              Spacing="8" Height="48">
                                      <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding PreviewPhotos}">
                                          <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                              <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                                  <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" />
                                              </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                          </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                          <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                              <DataTemplate>
                                                  <Border Width="48" Height="48" CornerRadius="8"
                                                          ClipToBounds="True"
                                                          BorderThickness="1"
                                                          Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                                          BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Slate200}">
                                                      <!-- 96 for a 48-pixel tile: two times the drawn size, so a card that lands on a
                                                                 high-density screen is not scaling a 48-pixel bitmap back up. -->
                                                      <Image Stretch="UniformToFill"
                                                             Source="{Binding Converter={StaticResource FilePathToBitmap}, ConverterParameter=96}" />
                                                  </Border>
                                              </DataTemplate>
                                          </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                      </ItemsControl>

                                      <Border Width="48" Height="48" CornerRadius="8"
                                              Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                              IsVisible="{Binding RemainingPhotoCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}">
                                          <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="0"
                                                      HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                                      VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                              <TextBlock Text="+" Classes="t11Semi"
                                                         Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}" />
                                              <TextBlock Text="{Binding RemainingPhotoCount}"
                                                         Classes="t11Semi"
                                                         Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}" />
                                          </StackPanel>
                                      </Border>
                                  </StackPanel>

                                <!-- Two numbers side by side, each behind its own glyph, the figure in bold and
                                     the unit after it. They sit on one row on purpose: stacked,
                                     the card grows by a line and the two numbers stop being
                                     comparable at a glance, which is all they are there for. -->
                                <Border Height="1" Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                        Margin="0,16,0,0" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Orientation="Horizontal"
                                                Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE82D;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                                                   FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                                        <TextBlock Classes="t12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate600}">
                                            <Run Text="Книг: " />
                                            <Run Text="{Binding BookCount, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                 FontWeight="Bold"
                                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate800}" />
                                            <Run Text=" шт." FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                        </TextBlock>
                                    </StackPanel>

                                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal"
                                                Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE8B9;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                                                   FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                                        <TextBlock Classes="t12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate600}">
                                            <Run Text="Разворотов: " />
                                            <Run Text="{Binding PageCount, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                 FontWeight="Bold"
                                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate800}" />
                                            <Run Text=" стр." FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                        </TextBlock>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Grid>

                                <!-- footer: the card's own width of "open", and the one
                                     destructive thing on it -->

                                <Border Height="1" Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                        Margin="0,16,0,0" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                    <Button Grid.Column="0" Classes="secondary" Padding="12,8"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Открыть проект"
                                            Command="{Binding DataContext.OpenProjectCommand, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=UserControl}}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="Открыть проект" Classes="t12Semi" />
                                    </Button>

                                    <Button Grid.Column="1" Classes="icon" Margin="8,0,0,0"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Удалить проект"
                                            Command="{Binding DataContext.DeleteProjectCommand, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=UserControl}}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE74D;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                                                   FontSize="14"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>
                                </StackPanel>
                        </Border>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>
                </Border>
            </ScrollViewer>
        </Panel>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
